ONE PROCESS APPROACH
:::
::: {.aoa-heading}
Authorship entitlement is not the same as opportunity to qualify
:::
:::

::: {.aoa-content}
::: {.process-grid}
::: {.process-card}
<div class="process-number">01</div>
<div class="process-title">Identify contributors</div>
Clinicians whose care substantially generated the cohort are named early.
:::
::: {.process-card}
<div class="process-number">02</div>
<div class="process-title">Invite into the science</div>
Before analysis is final, they are invited to working sessions about the question, data, interpretation, and manuscript story.
:::
::: {.process-card}
<div class="process-number">03</div>
<div class="process-title">Make expectations explicit</div>
Clinical contribution alone does not guarantee authorship; substantive intellectual contribution can create a path to qualify.
:::
::: {.process-card}
<div class="process-number">04</div>
<div class="process-title">Let contribution decide</div>
People who engage meaningfully can become authors. People who do not are acknowledged appropriately.
:::
:::

::: {.aoa-bottom-line}
This is not a rule. It is one way to make the pathway visible before the manuscript is already finished.
:::
:::
:::

::: {.notes}
Use the FIRST/FIERCE experience as an example without making it self-centered. “Here is one approach we tried.” It maps to the eventual framework: earlier, explicit, transparent, revisited.
:::


